{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 55996, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 4]], "date-time": "2026-06-04T01:56:27Z", "timestamp": 1780538187455, "version": "3.54.1"}, "reference-count": 36, "publisher": "American Association for the Advancement of Science (AAAS)", "issue": "5537", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Science"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2001, 9, 14]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>We demonstrate the protection of one bit of quantum information against all collective noise in three nuclear spins. Because no subspace of states offers this protection, the quantum bit was encoded in a proper noiseless subsystem. We therefore realize a general and efficient method for protecting quantum information. Robustness was verified for a full set of noise operators that do not distinguish the spins. Verification relied on the most complete exploration of engineered decoherence to date. The achieved fidelities show improved information storage for a large, noncommutative set of errors.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1126/science.1064460", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2002, 7, 27]], "date-time": "2002-07-27T09:52:08Z", "timestamp": 1027763528000}, "page": "2059-2063", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 202, "title": ["Experimental Realization of Noiseless Subsystems for Quantum Information Processing"], "prefix": "10.1126", "volume": "293", "author": [{"given": "Lorenza", "family": "Viola", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Los Alamos National Laboratory, Los Alamos, NM 87545, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Evan M.", "family": "Fortunato", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Nuclear Engineering, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge, MA 02139, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Marco A.", "family": "Pravia", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Nuclear Engineering, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge, MA 02139, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Emanuel", "family": "Knill", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Los Alamos National Laboratory, Los Alamos, NM 87545, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Raymond", "family": "Laflamme", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Los Alamos National Laboratory, Los Alamos, NM 87545, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "David G.", "family": "Cory", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Nuclear Engineering, Massachusetts Institute of Technology, Cambridge, MA 02139, USA."}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "221", "reference": [{"key": "e_1_3_1_2_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1126/science.273.5278.1073"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_3_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/35005001"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_4_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1109/18.720553"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_5_2", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "unstructured": "W. H. Zurek Phys. Today 40 (no. 10) 36 (1991).", "DOI": "10.1063/1.881293"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_6_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1098/rspa.1998.0167"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_7_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.79.3306"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_8_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.79.1953"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_9_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.2594"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_10_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevA.63.022306"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_11_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.84.2525"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_12_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.85.3520"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_13_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevA.63.012301"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_14_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.82.4556"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_15_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevA.63.042307"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_16_2", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "unstructured": "D. P. DiVincenzo D. Bacon J. Kempe G. Burkard K. B. Whaley Nature 408 (2000).", "DOI": "10.1038/35042541"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_17_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.87.077901"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_18_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1126/science.290.5491.498"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_19_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1126/science.1057357"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_19_3", "unstructured": "; published online 5 January 2001 (10.1126/science.1057357)."}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_20_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1088/0305-4470/34/35/331"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_21_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevA.54.2614"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_22_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1080/09500349708231894"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_23_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/23891"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_24_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1002/1521-3978(200009)48:9/11<875::AID-PROP875>3.0.CO;2-V"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_25_2", "unstructured": "We explicitly verified this assumption by tomographically reconstructing the super-operator corresponding to the process ε 0 ns (see Table 1 for definition). We found a maximum absolute deviation from identity | − ε 0 ns ()| ∼ 4%."}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_26_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.86.5845"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_27_2", "unstructured": "Optimization of the fidelity with respect to the intended 1-spin p.p. state for the data carbon alone results in an amount of identity component that is equal to the one based on the corresponding 3-spin p.p. state within the experimental accuracy."}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_28_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0079-6565(98)00021-1"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_29_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1016/S0375-9601(01)00083-4"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_30_2", "unstructured": "For a given species e.g. 13 C the gradient action is symmetric to an accuracy better than 0.1%. By contrast dephasing processes naturally occurring in alanine are dominated by noncollective effects reflecting the different chemical environment of each carbon."}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_31_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.2152"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_32_2", "unstructured": "We initially fit the data to a multiexponential model F e = Σ n  A n exp(− n 2 t ev /τ) + B that accounts for the possible single double and triple ( n = 1 2 3) decay modes of quantum coherences in a 3-spin system. From the resulting best estimates we confirm that contributions from double ( A 2 ) and triple ( A 3 ) quantum coherence terms arising from unintentionally populated states outside ℋ 1/2 are negligibly small."}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_33_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevA.54.3824"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_34_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/30156"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_35_2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.4752"}, {"key": "e_1_3_1_36_2", "unstructured": "This work was supported by the National Security Agency and Advanced Research and Development Activity (Army Research Office contract DAAD19-01-1-0519) by the Defense Sciences Office of the Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency (contract MDA972-01-1-0003) and by the Department of Energy (contract W-7405-ENG-36). We thank G. Teklemariam and N. Boulant for help with implementation and G. Boutis R. Onofrio T. Havel and S. Lloyd for valuable discussions."}], "container-title": ["Science"], "language": "en", "link": [{"URL": "https://www.science.org/doi/pdf/10.1126/science.1064460", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2024, 1, 9]], "date-time": "2024-01-09T22:15:51Z", "timestamp": 1704838551000}, "score": 133.6967, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.1064460"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2001, 9, 14]]}, "references-count": 36, "journal-issue": {"issue": "5537", "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2001, 9, 14]]}}, "alternative-id": ["10.1126/science.1064460"], "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1064460", "ISSN": ["0036-8075", "1095-9203"], "issn-type": [{"value": "0036-8075", "type": "print"}, {"value": "1095-9203", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2001, 9, 14]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 4, 22]], "date-time": "2026-04-22T04:28:02Z", "timestamp": 1776832082985, "version": "3.51.2"}, "reference-count": 53, "publisher": "American Physical Society (APS)", "issue": "6", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2003, 6, 19]], "date-time": "2003-06-19T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1055980800000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://link.aps.org/licenses/aps-default-license"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["Phys. Rev. A"], "DOI": "10.1103/physreva.67.062303", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2003, 6, 20]], "date-time": "2003-06-20T00:24:39Z", "timestamp": 1056068679000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 27, "title": ["Exploring noiseless subsystems via nuclear magnetic resonance"], "prefix": "10.1103", "volume": "67", "author": [{"given": "Evan M.", "family": "Fortunato", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Lorenza", "family": "Viola", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Marco A.", "family": "Pr